  "summary": "On 14 June 1985 Belgium, France, West Germany, Luxembourg and the Netherlands signed an agreement at Schengen, Luxembourg, on gradually abolishing checks at their common borders. It was concluded outside the EEC framework and was later supplemented by a 1990 convention and brought into EU law by the 1997 Treaty of Amsterdam.",
